board: wave 97 -- close #83 into #38 mechanism 1, retire three dead rows

#83 was the tick's only FAIL: dispatchable-and-undispatched. It had in fact
already been answered twice by lane.blit83 and lane.blit83b, neither of which
had a territory row while it ran, so the board could not see the coverage.

Board requests 1-4 from issuecomment-5737991240, applied:

  - #83 -> closed-duplicate of #38 mechanism 1. The premise was a COLUMN
    MISREAD: "each 1 px low" was the max_rgb column of rows whose differing
    column read 1,650, propagated through the title, the prediction JSON, a
    commit message and an investigation doc without ever being re-derived
    from a scored row. The falsifier the first pass named was run: 0 of 8
    blitted destination pixels differ on device at 71c7bd1d7d/24a75d6e3c, and
    the single survivor is (176,180) in all eight captures while the blit
    destination varies over eight coordinates.
  - #83 blocked_on: the sentence "now measured rather than argued" is
    WITHDRAWN. The control leg was inert by construction -- #38's diff is
    entirely inside the BLEND_AND arm of an if, and the SRCCOPY memmove last
    changed in 24087af22a -- so the arm restated the claim rather than testing
    it. #38's PASS is unaffected; it rests on 21 live expect-values.
  - #38 status_note: mechanism 1's residue on Image blit is one pixel and it
    is the last one. Not a re-judgement.
  - disposition stays 'defect'. The vocabulary has no not-in-this-component
    value and #75 was closed the same way; the defect is real and it is #38's.

